@database "todo"
@author "Enrico Ehrich"
@$VER: todo.guide 1.0 (29.09.2026)
@smartwrap

@node main "Todo"
@{h1}Todo

An agent working on something bigger than one answer keeps a task list
here: it breaks the work into tasks, marks what it is on, what depends on
what, and what is done. Each chat session has its own list. You see it in
the @{b}Todos@{ub} panel and can start, complete or delete tasks there
yourself; an optional hook keeps the open tasks in front of the model.

@{image docs/panel.png "The Todos panel with the tasks of a session"}

@{code}
For users
  @{"  The Todos panel  " link panel}

For agents and developers
  @{"  The todo tool  " link tool}
  @{"  Duplicates and dependencies  " link rules}
  @{"  The task-list hook  " link hook}
  @{"  What the model sees  " link model}
  @{"  Setting it up  " link setup}
@{body}
@endnode

@node panel "The Todos panel"
@{h1}The Todos panel

Open it from the launcher (@{b}Agents & tools@{ub}, "Todos"), or from a
session's info button, which opens it on that session.

@{image docs/panel.png "The Todos panel"}

@{h2}Which list it shows

The panel follows the chat: it shows the tasks of the session open there
and switches when you switch sessions. Opened from a session's info button
it is pinned to that session instead -- the toolbar says so ("Session
...") and @{b}Follow the chat@{ub} lets go of it. With no session open it
says so and shows nothing. The list reloads every 5 seconds; the menu next
to the reload button sets another interval or turns it off.

@{h2}What you see

@{bullet}The figures at the top: all tasks, and how many are not started,
in progress, blocked, cancelled and completed, with the share completed.
@{bullet}Two filters, by status and by priority, and how many tasks they
leave.
@{bullet}Each task with its status, id, title, priority, age, tags,
description and progress, what it depends on and what it blocks. A task
not started that waits on an unfinished one is marked @{i}waiting@{ui}.

@{h2}What you can do

@{table}
Button | Shown on | Does
Start | a task not started that waits on nothing | sets it in progress
Complete | a task in progress, blocked or waiting | sets it completed; tasks waiting on it become free
Delete | a task no other task depends on | removes it, after asking
@{body}

An agent may change the same task a moment earlier. When the server refuses
a click -- the task is gone, has gained a dependent, or is no longer in a
state the button takes -- the panel shows the reason and loads the list
anew.
@endnode

@node tool "The todo tool"
@{h1}The todo tool

The plugin gives an agent one tool, named like the plugin instance
(@{tt}todo@{utt} in the default setup). Every call names an
@{tt}operation@{utt}; the tasks belong to the session the agent runs in. A
sub-agent runs in a session of its own and so keeps a list of its own.

@{h2}Operations

@{table}
operation | Needs | Does
create | title | a new task; see @{" Duplicates and dependencies " link rules}
update | task_id | changes status, progress, priority, tags, dependencies, adds a note
get | task_id | one task with what blocks it and what it blocks
list | -- | tasks by filter, oldest first
delete | task_id | removes a task; with dependents only with cascade
summary | -- | counts, overall progress and the next tasks to take
@{body}

@{h2}Parameters

@{table}
Parameter | Used by | Meaning
title | create | up to 200 characters
description | create | up to 2000 characters
priority | create, update | low, medium, high, critical; a create without it is medium
tags | create, update | on update the tags are added; none is removed
depends_on | create, update | task ids; on update the list replaces the old one
status | update | not-started, in-progress, completed, blocked, cancelled
progress | update | 0 to 100
note | update | appended to the task's notes with a timestamp
allow_duplicates | create | true: no duplicate check
idempotency_key | create | the same key returns the task made with it, whatever its title
filter_status, filter_priority | list | lists of values; a task matches one of them
filter_tags | list | a task matches when it has one of the tags
only_unblocked | list | leave out tasks with an unfinished dependency
limit, offset | list | a page of the result
cascade | delete | also delete every task that depends on this one
@{body}

@{h2}Answers

An answer that changes or refuses something carries a @{tt}status@{utt}: @{tt}created@{utt},
@{tt}exists@{utt} (a duplicate or a known idempotency key: the existing
task, with @{tt}reason@{utt}), @{tt}updated@{utt}, @{tt}deleted@{utt} (with
@{tt}cascade_deleted@{utt}), @{tt}not_found@{utt}, @{tt}rejected@{utt}
(a delete with dependents: @{tt}dependent_tasks@{utt}),
@{tt}limit_reached@{utt} or @{tt}validation_failed@{utt} with a
@{tt}message@{utt} saying what to change. @{tt}get@{utt} and
@{tt}update@{utt} add @{tt}dependency_info@{utt} (@{tt}blocked_by@{utt},
@{tt}blocking@{utt}); @{tt}list@{utt} adds counts and
@{tt}has_more@{utt}/@{tt}next_offset@{utt} for paging;
@{tt}summary@{utt} gives @{tt}by_status@{utt}, @{tt}by_priority@{utt},
@{tt}overall_progress@{utt} (the mean progress), @{tt}completion_rate@{utt}
and @{tt}next_unblocked@{utt}: up to five tasks not started and free,
highest priority first. @{tt}get@{utt}, @{tt}list@{utt} and
@{tt}summary@{utt} return their data without a status. A status or filter
value the tool does not know, or a title over 200 characters, fails the
call with an error.

@{h2}An example

@{code json}
{"operation": "create", "title": "Write the migration", "priority": "high"}
{"operation": "create", "title": "Run the migration on staging", "depends_on": ["task_001"]}
{"operation": "update", "task_id": "task_001", "status": "completed", "note": "Reviewed"}
{"operation": "list", "only_unblocked": true}
@{body}

Task ids are made by the plugin (@{tt}task_001@{utt}, @{tt}task_002@{utt},
...). An agent uses the id an answer returned, never one it expects.
@endnode

@node rules "Duplicates and dependencies"
@{h1}Duplicates and dependencies

@{h2}Duplicates

Models tend to create the same task twice, so @{tt}create@{utt} compares
the title with every task not completed (cancelled ones count):

@{bullet}95 % alike or more: nothing is created; the answer is the existing
task with @{tt}status: exists@{utt}, @{tt}reason: duplicate_title@{utt}
and the similarity.
@{bullet}80 to 95 % alike: the task is created. The answer does not
mention the similar one; only the log does.
@{bullet}An @{tt}idempotency_key@{utt} is checked first, against all
tasks: a retry with the same key returns the first task.

@{tt}allow_duplicates: true@{utt} skips the title check, for tasks that
are alike on purpose ("Review PR 123", "Review PR 124").

@{h2}Dependencies

A dependency must be an existing task, and no chain may lead back to the
task itself; either is refused with a message. @{tt}blocked@{utt} is kept
by the plugin, not set by hand:

@{bullet}A task created with an unfinished dependency starts
@{tt}blocked@{utt}.
@{bullet}A task in progress becomes @{tt}blocked@{utt} when one of its
dependencies is no longer complete.
@{bullet}A blocked task becomes @{tt}not-started@{utt} again when all its
dependencies are complete.
@{bullet}Setting @{tt}blocked@{utt} by hand is refused while nothing
blocks the task.

A task not started that is given a dependency later stays not started;
the panel marks it @{i}waiting@{ui}, and @{tt}only_unblocked@{utt} leaves
it out. Set in progress through the tool, it turns @{tt}blocked@{utt} at
once.

@{h2}Statuses

Any status can follow any other; the plugin keeps the times and the
progress with them. The first @{tt}in-progress@{utt} sets
@{tt}started_at@{utt}; @{tt}completed@{utt} sets @{tt}completed_at@{utt}
and progress 100; leaving it clears @{tt}completed_at@{utt} again, the
progress stays until it is set.
@endnode

@node hook "The task-list hook"
@{h1}The task-list hook

@{tt}inject_todo_tasks@{utt} runs before each LLM call and puts the open
tasks in front of the model, so it does not have to call the tool to know
where it stands. It is off until an agent switches it on.

@{h2}What the model gets

A message at the end of the history, from the plugin: a short reminder of
the tool and the tasks, one line each with status, id, title, priority and
progress, and what they depend on and block. With no tasks yet only the
reminder. It is added only when it differs from the last one the hook
added -- the conversation grows by a list when the list changes, and the
cached prompt in front of it stays as it was.

@{code markdown}
## TODO Tool Available

Use `todo()` to break down and track your work. ...

**Current active tasks:**

- ⏳ **task_002**: Implement the model [🔴 CRIT, 40%]
  - Depends on: task_001
  - Blocks: task_003
- 🚫 **task_003**: Write the tests [🟡 MED, 0%]
  - Depends on: task_002
@{body}

@{h2}Switching it on

In the agent's YAML; its settings go in the same place:

@{code yaml}
agent_config:
  hooks:
    enabled: true
    overrides:
      todo.inject_todo_tasks:
        enabled: true
        max_tasks: 10
@{body}

@{h2}Settings

@{table}
Key | Default | Meaning
max_tasks | 20 | how many tasks the list shows: the oldest first
filter_status | not-started, in-progress, blocked | which tasks it shows
include_completed | false | true: every task, whatever its status
format | markdown | markdown, or text for one plain line per task
@{body}

The defaults come from the plugin; a @{tt}hook_config:@{utt} block in the
plugin's server entry changes them for every agent, and an agent's own
override wins over both.
@endnode

@node model "What the model sees"
@{h1}What the model sees

@{h2}The tool

The tool description and every parameter's description come from the
plugin's @{tt}schema.yaml@{utt}. A refused call answers with a status and a
@{tt}message@{utt} that says what to change, for example "UPDATE operation
requires 'task_id' parameter", "Cannot manually set status to 'blocked'
..." or "Cannot delete task task_002: 1 task(s) depend on it. Use
cascade=True to delete all: task_003". The chat's status line ends with
the result: "Created task_004 (blocked): ...", "Updated task_002: status,
progress", "Listed 3 task(s)".

@{h2}Tokens and cache

Tool answers are ordinary tool results: appended, nothing earlier changes.
A @{tt}list@{utt} without @{tt}limit@{utt} returns every matching task
with its description -- on a long list, filter or page. The hook appends
its list at the end of the history and only when the list changed; it
never rewrites the system prompt or an earlier message.

@{h2}Known gaps

@{bullet}Tags can be added, not removed.
@{bullet}@{tt}depends_on@{utt} on update replaces the whole list; to add
one dependency, send the old ones with it.
@{bullet}With more open tasks than @{tt}max_tasks@{utt}, the hook shows
the oldest; the newest wait until older ones are done.
@endnode

@node setup "Setting it up"
@{h1}Setting it up

The plugin is on in the default configuration:

@{code yaml}
plugins:
  servers:
    todo:
      type: todo
      enabled: true
@{body}

An agent sees the tool when its allowlist names it:

@{code yaml}
agent_config:
  tools:
    allowed:
      - "+todo/*"
@{body}

@{h2}Server settings

@{table}
Key | Default | Meaning
storage_path | todos in the data directory | where the task lists are kept
max_tasks_per_session | 1000 | a create beyond it answers limit_reached
enable_dependencies | true | false: nothing is blocked; a dependency must still exist
auto_save | true | write each change to disk at once
max_cache_size | 50 | sessions kept in memory; the rest are read from disk when asked
@{body}

Each session's tasks are one JSON file, named after the session, in the
storage folder. A session the plugin holds in memory writes its file anew
on the next change: delete a file only while the server is stopped.
@endnode
